   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Trooper Martin J. Kerins Memorial Bridge\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8512",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8512-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 3,
       "fullName": "Alexis Weik",
       "imgName": "1310_Alexis_Weik.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1493,
       "sessionMemberId": 1848,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "WEIK"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-n, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8512\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Trooper Martin J. Kerins Memorial\nBridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to honor the life and ultimate sacrifice of\nNew York State Police Trooper Martin J. Kerins.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n  Section  1.  amends  the  highway law by adding a new section 344-n to\nprovide that the portion of the state highway  system  constituting  the\nbridge  on county route three, exits number 35 on the east and westbound\nSouthern state parkway in the town of Babylon, county of Suffolk, to  be\nknown as the \"State Trooper Martin J. Kerins Memorial Bridge\".\n\n  Section  2.  provides  for  the  installation  and  maintenance of the\nsignage.\n\n  Section 3. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation pays tribute to State  Trooper  Martin  J.  Kerins  who\ntragically  lost  his life on August 23'1, 1938 in Babylon, NY by desig-\nnating the portion of the state highway system constituting the Southern\nState Parkway Weliwood Ave. overpass on route 3, in the Town of Babylon,\nSuffolk County, as the \"State Trooper Martin J. Kerins Memorial Bridge\".\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on immediately.\n",
